  "id": "COMPOUND:39549 - PROTEIN:1493",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 3-Hydroxymollugin may interact with the Prostaglandin E2 receptor EP4 subtype through multiple pathways. The drug is implicated in targeting fusion glycoprotein F0, which is a target of 4-[(6,7-Dimethoxy-2-Methyl-3,4-Dihydro-1H-Isoquinolin-1-Yl)Methyl]Phenol and cis-Isopinocamphone, both of which are known to interact with the EP4 receptor. Additionally, 3-Hydroxymollugin is also shown to target Asialoglycoprotein receptor 2, which is a target of (+)-Actinidine, which in turn targets the EP4 receptor. These findings collectively indicate that 3-Hydroxymollugin may exert its biological effects through a network of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to modulation of the EP4 receptor. The evidence is consistent with the hypothesis that 3-Hydroxymollugin could act as a modulator of the EP4 receptor, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
